I. Heat losses are reduced because the currents are small.
II. Thin wires can be used because small currents are flowing.
III. The power can flow faster because the voltage is high.', null, '["I only","I and II only","II and III only","I and III only","I, II and III"]', 1, 'Heat loss in the cables is I²R, so a smaller current reduces it (I), and a smaller current also allows thinner wires (II). Power does not flow ''faster'' at high voltage (III).', true, '2026-10-12 19:15:16.93', '2026-10-12 19:15:16.93', null, null, null, 'It is usual to transmit electric power at high voltage and low current. Which of the following are possible advantages of the method?<br>I. Heat losses are reduced because the currents are small.<br>II. Thin wires can be used because small currents are flowing.<br>III. The power can flow faster because the voltage is high.', '["I only","I and II only","II and III only","I and III only","I, II and III"]', 'Heat loss in the cables is I<sup>2</sup>R, so a smaller current reduces it (I), and a smaller current also allows thinner wires (II). Power does not flow ''faster'' at high voltage (III).', '{"bold":[],"italic":[],"underline":[],"fillBlanks":[]}');
