I. There is a tension on the water surface.
II. Kerosene reduces the density of water so that the needle becomes denser than water.
III. Kerosene reduces the surface tension of water.', null, '["I only","II only","III only","I and II","I and III"]', 4, 'The needle floats because of surface tension (I). Kerosene lowers the surface tension (III), so the surface can no longer support the needle.', true, '2026-10-12 19:15:19.397', '2026-10-12 19:15:19.397', null, null, null, 'A small steel needle is carefully floated on water in a beaker. When a few drops of kerosene are introduced into the water the needle sinks. Which of the following statements correctly explain(s) the observation?<br>I. There is a tension on the water surface.<br>II. Kerosene reduces the density of water so that the needle becomes denser than water.<br>III. Kerosene reduces the surface tension of water.', '["I only","II only","III only","I and II","I and III"]', 'The needle floats because of surface tension (I). Kerosene lowers the surface tension (III), so the surface can no longer support the needle.', '{"bold":[],"italic":[],"underline":[],"fillBlanks":[]}');
I. All metallic surfaces emit the same number of photoelectrons in a given light.
II. Most metallic surfaces emit photoelectrons in visible and infrared light.
III. A metallic surface emits photoelectrons if the frequency of the incident light is higher than its own characteristic threshold frequency.', null, '["I only","II only","I and II","II and III","III only"]', 2, 'III is true. I is false because the number emitted depends on the metal and the light intensity. II is false because most metals need ultraviolet light, whose frequency is above their threshold.', true, '2026-10-12 19:15:20.385', '2026-10-12 19:15:20.385', null, null, null, 'Which of the following statements is (are) <b>NOT</b> true about the emission of photoelectrons from metallic surfaces?<br>I. All metallic surfaces emit the same number of photoelectrons in a given light.<br>II. Most metallic surfaces emit photoelectrons in visible and infrared light.<br>III. A metallic surface emits photoelectrons if the frequency of the incident light is higher than its own characteristic threshold frequency.', '["I only","II only","I and II","II and III","III only"]', 'III is true. I is false because the number emitted depends on the metal and the light intensity. II is false because most metals need ultraviolet light, whose frequency is above their threshold.', '{"bold":["NOT"],"italic":[],"underline":[],"fillBlanks":[]}');
I. A liquid boils when its saturated vapour pressure is equal to the external pressure.
II. Dissolved substances in pure water lead to an increase in the boiling point.
III. When the external pressure is increased, the boiling point increases.
IV. Dissolved substances in pure water decrease the boiling point.', null, '["I, II and III","I, II, III and IV","I, II and IV","II, III and IV."]', 0, 'I, II and III are correct. Dissolved impurities raise the boiling point of water, so IV is wrong.', true, '2026-10-12 19:15:47.501', '2026-10-12 19:15:47.501', null, null, null, 'Which combination of the following are peculiarities of the boiling point of a liquid?<br>I. A liquid boils when its saturated vapour pressure is equal to the external pressure.<br>II. Dissolved substances in pure water lead to an increase in the boiling point.<br>III. When the external pressure is increased, the boiling point increases.<br>IV. Dissolved substances in pure water decrease the boiling point.', '["I, II and III","I, II, III and IV","I, II and IV","II, III and IV."]', 'I, II and III are correct. Dissolved impurities raise the boiling point of water, so IV is wrong.', '{"bold":[],"italic":[],"underline":[],"fillBlanks":[]}');
I. It absorbs only the green component of sunlight.
II. It absorbs all colours in sunlight except green.
