V. The first harmonic of a note has double the frequency of the fundamental note.', null, '["I and II","II and III","I and II","III and IV","IV and V"]', 1, 'II is wrong: intensity is proportional to the square of the amplitude. III is wrong: beats come from the interference of two waves of slightly different frequencies, not from one wave travelling faster. I is correct, and IV is correct (beat frequency = 502 - 500 = 2 Hz).', true, '2026-10-12 19:15:16.548', '2026-10-12 19:15:16.548', null, null, null, 'Which of the following is <b>NOT</b> correct?<br>I. The pitch of a sound note depends on the frequency of vibrations.<br>II. The intensity of a sound note is proportional to the amplitude of vibrations.<br>III. Beats are produced by two sources of sound because one wave is travelling faster than the other.<br>IV. When two sources of sound of frequencies 500 Hz and 502 Hz are sounded together, a beat frequency of 2 Hz is observed.<br>V. The first harmonic of a note has double the frequency of the fundamental note.', '["I and II","II and III","I and II","III and IV","IV and V"]', 'II is wrong: intensity is proportional to the square of the amplitude. III is wrong: beats come from the interference of two waves of slightly different frequencies, not from one wave travelling faster. I is correct, and IV is correct (beat frequency = 502 - 500 = 2 Hz).', '{"bold":["NOT"],"italic":[],"underline":[],"fillBlanks":[]}');
